From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:11:36 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 23/27] server/llama : cheaper conversation switches (prompt
 cache save/restore)

With one slot and several clients, a request for another conversation
first saves the slot's state to the --cache-ram prompt cache and may
restore another one. Env switches, default off, outputs unchanged:
- LLAMA_PCACHE_POOL: cache entries live in reused pinned host blocks
  (counted against --cache-ram); no fresh zero-filled allocation per
  save, restores upload at link speed
- LLAMA_PCACHE_CKPT_MOVE: checkpoints the slot would drop are moved
  into the cache entry instead of copied
- LLAMA_PCACHE_KEEP: keep the host copy after a restore and save only
  the recurrent state and changed KV rows (=2 verifies every save and
  restore byte for byte)
- LLAMA_SWITCH_PROF: one timestamped log line per request stage

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
